 "source": "# Inline tables: `{ key = value, ... }`. taplo never breaks between the key-value\n# pairs — it only breaks an *array value* inside one. A long inline table of pure\n# scalars stays on one line even when it overflows. Nested inline tables exercise\n# the brace matching.\n\npoint = { x = 1, y = 2 }\n\nmetadata = { name = \"example\", version = \"1.0.0\", authors = [\"a\", \"b\"], license = \"MIT\" }\n\nlong_inline = { host = \"db.example.com\", port = 5432, ssl = true, timeout = 30, retries = 3 }\n\nnested = { outer = { inner = { deep = \"value\" } }, sibling = 2 }\n\nmixed = { array = [1, 2, 3], table = { key = \"value\" }, scalar = 42 }\n",
